  18, 19, 20], "studies": [{"study_index": 1, "title": "Nadroparin for the prevention of thromboembolic events in       
  ambulatory patients with metastatic or locally advanced solid cancer receiving chemotherapy: a randomised,            
  placebo-controlled, double-blind study", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Clinical trials are needed to assess the clinical    
  benefit of antithrombotic prophylaxis in patients with cancer who are receiving chemotherapy, since these patients    
  are at an increased risk of developing a thromboembolism. We did a trial to assess the clinical benefit of the        
