of venous thromboembolism (VTE), bleeding complications are a challenge in clinical practice. This review article       
focuses on the overall bleeding risk of cancer patients and the risk of major and clinically relevant bleeding          
associated with anticoagulant treatment, such as vitamin K antagonists, LMWH and the direct oral anticoagulants. It also
